d paper inspection record or an electronic inspection record signed by the inspecting officer. Each record must identify the display, the inspection date, and every public exit inspected.\",\"references\":[],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:a4296585bbc7c92415a0d873a686b49f41fda3b668ad128f86a8eca38a5b421e\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(a) For a temporary display open to the public after sunset on agency premises, the organizer must satisfy all of the following conditions:\",\"(4) Before admitting the first visitor, the organizer must give the agency either a signed paper inspection record or an electronic inspection record signed by the inspecting officer. Each record must identify the display, the inspection date, and every public exit inspected.\"],\"scope_text\":\"For each inspection record given to the agency before admitting the first visitor to a temporary display open to the public after sunset on agency premises.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":756,\"summary\":\"Each inspection record provided to the agency must identify the display, the inspection date, and every public exit inspected.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
